---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Connections from '../components/Connections.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import {current,groups} from '../lib/connections';
import Code from '../components/Code.astro';
import WorksWith from '../components/WorksWith.astro';
import {githubUrl,defaultBranch} from '../lib/links.mjs';
import snippets from '../../../../docs/onboarding/snippets.json';
const worker='https://slurp.YOUR-SUBDOMAIN.workers.dev';
const feedbackMount=`import { init } from '@hitslop/slurp-sdk';\nimport { mountFeedback } from '@hitslop/slurp-sdk/feedback';\n\ninit({ endpoint: 'YOUR_INGEST_URL', key: 'YOUR_PUBLISHABLE_KEY' });\nmountFeedback({ askEmail: true });`;
const webhooksShort='slurp project webhook prj_… github\nslurp project webhook prj_… revenuecat\nslurp project webhook prj_… stripe --secret whsec_…\nslurp project webhook prj_… generic';
const feedbackQuery="slurp sync\nslurp sql \"SELECT timestamp, data->>'message' AS message, data->>'rating' AS rating FROM events WHERE event = 'feedback' ORDER BY timestamp DESC\"";
const fill=(t:string)=>t.replaceAll('YOUR_INGEST_URL',worker+'/v1/events').replaceAll('YOUR_ORIGIN',worker).replaceAll('YOUR_HOST',worker.replace('https://','')).replaceAll('YOUR_PROJECT_ID','prj_…').replaceAll('YOUR_PUBLISHABLE_KEY','slurp_pk_…');
const recipes=[['Where the endpoint and key come from','Both come from slurp init; there is nothing to sign up for','senders'],['JavaScript and TypeScript','npm install @hitslop/slurp-sdk','sdk'],['React Native and Expo','npm install @hitslop/slurp-react-native @react-native-async-storage/async-storage','reactNative'],['Swift (iOS, macOS)','Segment’s analytics-swift: set both apiHost and cdnHost to your Worker','swift'],['HTTP, any language','POST one JSON object with only an event name','http'],['Segment SDKs','Keep your SDK; your publishable key is the write key','segment'],['Sentry SDKs','Keep your SDK; change the DSN','sentry'],['Python','pip install segment-analytics-python or sentry-sdk; no Slurp package','python'],['Webhooks','Each command prints a URL and a secret to paste into the provider','webhooks']] as const;
const sections=[{id:'sdks',label:'Install an SDK'},{id:'feedback',label:'Feedback widget'},{id:'today',label:'Works today'},{id:'roadmap',label:'Exploring'},{id:'jev',label:'Jev'}];
---
<Page title="Connections" description="Current Slurp SDK, HTTP, and agent workflows, plus ideas being explored for future connections." current="connections" sections={sections}>
<header class="connections-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Connections</p><h1>Your app. Your tools.<br/><span class="hot">Your agent.</span></h1><p class="lede">Bring events home and work with them locally. Here’s what works today, and where we could take it next.</p></header>
<section id="sdks" class="section"><span class="section-number">01 / SDKS</span><h2>Install an SDK, or keep the one you have.</h2><p>Every path lands in the same archive and the same DuckDB table. <code>slurp init</code> creates your project and its first publishable key and prints that key with your ingest URL; the examples below show where each one goes.</p><WorksWith/><p class="notice">React Native is in preview.</p><p class="fine">Logos belong to their owners and show compatibility only.</p>{recipes.map(([title,how,key])=><div class="recipe"><h3>{title}</h3><p class="fine">{how}</p><Code label="Example" code={key==='webhooks'?webhooksShort:fill(snippets[key])}/></div>)}<p><a href={`${githubUrl}/blob/${defaultBranch}/docs/sdks.md`}>Every option, mapping and limit ↗</a></p></section>
<section id="feedback" class="section"><span class="section-number">02 / FEEDBACK WIDGET</span><h2>Let your users talk to you, from your own site.</h2><p>This site uses a custom feedback form powered by the Slurp SDK. The standard widget below is a ready-made alternative. Add it to any web page in a few lines: a small form (message, optional rating and email) that lands next to your other events, so your agent reads what people say beside what they did.</p>
<ol class="how-steps"><li><h3>Install</h3><p class="fine">The same package as the JavaScript SDK.</p><Code label="Terminal" code="npm install @hitslop/slurp-sdk"/></li>
<li><h3>Mount it</h3><p class="fine">Use the ingest URL and publishable key from <code>slurp init</code>. The key only adds events, so it is safe in a page.</p><Code label="Your page's script" code={fill(feedbackMount)}/></li>
<li><h3>Read it</h3><p class="fine">Each submission is a <code>feedback</code> event. Ask your agent, or query it after <code>slurp sync</code>.</p><Code label="Terminal" code={feedbackQuery}/></li></ol>
<h3>Make it yours</h3><dl class="options"><dt><code>askEmail: true</code></dt><dd>Ask for an optional email address, for people who want a reply.</dd><dt><code>data: () =&gt; ({'{'} plan {'}'})</code></dt><dd>Attach anything useful, read when the form is sent: the current screen, the plan, the release.</dd><dt><code>theme</code>, <code>accent</code>, <code>position</code></dt><dd><code>auto</code> follows the visitor's dark mode (or force <code>light</code> or <code>dark</code>); your brand colour; <code>bottom-left</code> or <code>bottom-right</code>.</dd><dt><code>label</code>, <code>title</code>, <code>placeholder</code>, <code>ratings</code></dt><dd>Your words on the button and the form, or no rating row.</dd><dt><code>button: false</code></dt><dd>Open it from your own button or menu with the <code>open()</code> that <code>mountFeedback</code> returns.</dd><dt><code>poweredBy: false</code></dt><dd>Hides the small "Powered by Slurp" link under the form (on by default).</dd></dl>
<p class="fine">Full reference: <a href={`${githubUrl}/blob/${defaultBranch}/sdks/js/README.md#feedback-widget`}>the SDK readme</a>.</p></section>
<section id="today" class="section"><span class="section-number">03 / WORKS TODAY</span><h2>Start with your app and your agent.</h2><p>Capture with an SDK, your existing Segment or Sentry SDK, or the HTTP API. New events are published as archives about every 10 minutes; sync them with the CLI, then let your agent query the local data. Agent entries describe CLI workflows. <a href="/agents/">Connect your coding agent, Grok Bot, or Muse with the setup guides.</a></p><Connections items={current}/></section>
<section id="roadmap" class="section"><span class="section-number">04 / EXPLORING</span><h2>More of your stack, together.</h2><p class="notice">Ideas we are exploring. Not available yet.</p>{groups.map(g=><section class="connection-group" id={g.id}><h3>{g.title}</h3><Connections items={g.items}/></section>)}</section>
<section id="jev" class="section"><span class="section-number">05 / JEV · EXPLORING</span><h2>Something that notices.</h2><p>Jev is an idea for classifying incoming events and routing useful signals to an agent. This workflow is illustrative; processing and alert delivery are not available.</p><div class="steps"><div><Icon name="connections"/><h3>Events arrive</h3><p>From your app and future connections.</p></div><div><Icon name="agent"/><h3>Jev classifies</h3><p>Identify a possible signal and its confidence.</p></div><div><Icon name="webhook"/><h3>Alerts go out</h3><p>Hand the evidence to an agent or endpoint.</p></div></div><p class="fine">Illustrative signals: a spike in export failures, a new error pattern, stalled onboarding, or possible churn.</p><a class="btn" href="/docs/">Get started with what works today ↗</a></section>
</Page>
<style>
.how-steps{list-style:none;counter-reset:step;display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr);gap:6px;margin:22px 0 8px;padding:0}
.how-steps>li{counter-increment:step;position:relative;min-width:0;padding-left:44px}
.how-steps>li::before{content:counter(step);position:absolute;left:0;top:2px;display:grid;place-items:center;width:30px;height:30px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--red);color:#fff;font:800 15px var(--display)}
.how-steps h3{margin:0 0 2px;font-size:17px}
.how-steps .fine{margin:0 0 4px}
.options{display:grid;grid-template-columns:max-content minmax(0,1fr);gap:10px 22px;margin:12px 0 18px;padding:16px 18px;border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:10px;background:#fcfdff;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5}
.options dt{font-weight:600}
.options dd{margin:0;color:var(--muted)}
@media(max-width:700px){.options{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:2px}.options dd{margin-bottom:10px}.how-steps>li{padding-left:38px}}
</style>
